          "needle": "Prepared the concrete"
        },
        {
          "firstLineText": "All13retirement edges are explicit, including transitive retirement of Read-only discovery. TX substitutes its exact discovery/limits/Directory, receipt/retained-key/reauthorization/recovery response vehicles while preserving lower laws it does not contradict. Inherited singleton semantics are checked through a TX receipt's single entry; aliases retain locator semantics. TX sequence remains ordered separately committing member transactions with partial progress/interleaving, never an atomic batch. The numeric same-value no-op row's RU-only no-receipts/noEvents citation remains scoped to RU: it cannot prohibit required TX receipts/Events or retire the numeric no-op obligation. Genuine RU inline results, per-member recovery and RU continuity still require their own separately bound RU cohort; their reports cannot prove TX inheritance.",
          "lines": [
            9
          ],
          "needle": "All13retirement"
        },
        {
          "firstLineText": "A further concrete source constraint is capacity: the current17row manifest is867,804bytes against TX's1,048,576byte ordinary cap, leaving180,772bytes. The4,194,304cumulative override belongs to RU only. Existing128depth/100000nodes/10000container bounds and exact5srequest/65536header/1MiBbody/2MiBwire session bounds are retained. The existing TXpositive63000ms and carrier data5s callbacks are unchanged. Final251 authored workload size, collection capacity, callbacks/outer supervision and cleanup scheduling are UNKNOWN, not extrapolated passes or failures. No cap/deadline widening, automatic retry, implicit shard/report union or new helper is supplied.",
          "lines": [
            17
          ],
          "needle": "A further concrete source constraint"
        },
        {
          "firstLineText": "Selected laws remain in the denominator when their owner, fixture or administration is absent. Historyfalse excludes only30optional History IDs; it does not waive mandatory TX framing, ledger/retained-copy acquisition, erasure or recovery. G06 preserves unsupported erasure/applied-ledger/logical-restore boundaries. The existing private pending-recovery seam offers a concrete next recipe: obtain an actual admitted pending receipt without executing it, controlled real process death, same-store createfalse recovery, old pending receipt nondisclosure and retry/replay exactly once with ordinary live continuity. That is setup/assurance plus later HTTP observation, not a new wire administration API, power-loss proof, erasure or logical-restore qualification. Other controlled-copy/import/restore routes and operator scope remain UNKNOWN. Root can continue independent preparation without asking a human now.",
          "lines": [
            19
          ],
          "needle": "Selected laws remain"
        }
